326	<body>
327	
328	<div class="deck" id="deck">
329	
330	  <!-- Slide 0: Title -->
331	  <div class="slide slide-dark slide-center active" data-index="0">
332	    <div class="eyebrow">harness-traj-weaver</div>
333	    <h1>Meta-Harness</h1>
334	    <p class="subtitle">The Self-Improving Loop for AI-Coded Software</p>
335	    <p style="margin-top:var(--sp-xxl);font-size:14px;color:var(--on-dark-soft)">Four principles · Four skills · One hook</p>
336	    <div class="keypoint">AI-coded software needs a self-reviewing harness, not just more tests</div>
337	  </div>
338	
339	  <!-- Slide 1: The Problem -->
340	  <div class="slide slide-left" data-index="1">
341	    <div class="eyebrow">The Problem</div>
342	    <h2>LLMs write code,<br>but who reviews the reviewer?</h2>
343	    <ul class="step-list" style="margin-top:var(--sp-lg)">
344	      <li><span class="step-num">01</span> AI generates code in Claude Code sessions</li>
345	      <li><span class="step-num">02</span> No trace between commit and the conversation that produced it</li>
346	      <li><span class="step-num">03</span> Review is reactive — after code is already committed</li>
347	      <li><span class="step-num">04</span> No feedback loop to improve the process itself</li>
348	    </ul>
349	    <div class="keypoint">Without traceability, AI-generated code is a black box — you can't diagnose what you can't see</div>
350	  </div>
351	
352	  <!-- Slide 2: Four Principles -->
353	  <div class="slide slide-center" data-index="2">
354	    <div class="eyebrow">The Foundation</div>
355	    <h2>Four Principles</h2>
356	    <div class="principles">
357	      <div class="principle">
358	        <div class="num">1</div>
359	        <h4>Filesystem as Memory</h4>
360	        <p>Full history on disk — no vector DB, no persistent memory. Just the filesystem.</p>
361	      </div>
362	      <div class="principle">
363	        <div class="num">2</div>
364	        <h4>Trace-Level Reasoning</h4>
365	        <p>Diagnose raw execution traces, not compressed summaries or aggregate scores.</p>
366	      </div>
367	      <div class="principle">
368	        <div class="num">3</div>
369	        <h4>Search-Set Feedback</h4>
370	        <p>All improvement signals from the search set. Never expose test-set results.</p>
371	      </div>
372	      <div class="principle">
373	        <div class="num">4</div>
374	        <h4>Self-Improving</h4>
375	        <p>Harness quality rises automatically as the underlying agent becomes more capable.</p>
376	      </div>
377	    </div>
378	    <div class="keypoint">These aren't abstract virtues — each principle maps to a concrete skill that enforces it</div>
379	  </div>
380	
381	  <!-- Slide 3: The Loop -->
382	  <div class="slide slide-dark slide-center" data-index="3">
383	    <div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--accent-amber)">Architecture</div>
384	    <h2>The Self-Improving Loop</h2>
385	    <div class="flow-row" style="margin-top:var(--sp-xl)">
386	      <div class="flow-node active">Filesystem</div>
387	      <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
388	      <div class="flow-node">Propose</div>
389	      <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
390	      <div class="flow-node">Harness + LLM</div>
391	      <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
392	      <div class="flow-node">Evaluate</div>
393	      <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
394	      <div class="flow-node">Feedback</div>
395	      <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
396	      <div class="flow-node active">Filesystem</div>
397	    </div>
398	    <p style="margin-top:var(--sp-xl);color:var(--on-dark-soft);font-size:15px">
399	      Agent proposes → Harness tests → Results flow back → Agent learns → repeat
400	    </p>
401	    <div class="keypoint">The filesystem is the only database — every artifact is a file you can read, diff, and learn from</div>
402	  </div>
403	
404	  <!-- Slide 4: Skills Overview -->
405	  <div class="slide slide-center" data-index="4">
406	    <div class="eyebrow">Implementation</div>
407	    <h2>Four Skills, One Loop</h2>
408	    <div class="skill-row">
409	      <div class="skill-card">
410	        <div class="icon">&#9655;</div>
411	        <h4>traj</h4>
412	        <p>Session trajectory visualization — interactive timeline from JSONL traces</p>
413	      </div>
414	      <div class="skill-card">
415	        <div class="icon">&#9733;</div>
416	        <h4>metric</h4>
417	        <p>Code review dashboard — Karpathy 4 principles auto-scoring</p>
418	      </div>
419	      <div class="skill-card">
420	        <div class="icon">&#9998;</div>
421	        <h4>survey</h4>
422	        <p>Human feedback forms — QA + paradigm assessment with git context</p>
423	      </div>
424	      <div class="skill-card">
425	        <div class="icon">&#9670;</div>
426	        <h4>theme</h4>
427	        <p>Visual design tokens — warm Anthropic aesthetic for all HTML output</p>
428	      </div>
429	    </div>
430	    <div class="keypoint">Four skills, each covering one step of the loop — together they close the feedback cycle</div>
431	  </div>
432	
433	  <!-- Slide 5: traj — Observe -->
434	  <div class="slide slide-left" data-index="5">
435	    <div class="eyebrow">Principle #2 &mdash; Trace-Level Reasoning</div>
436	    <h2>traj: See What the Agent Saw</h2>
437	    <p style="color:var(--muted);max-width:700px">Reads Claude Code JSONL sessions and generates a self-contained interactive timeline with TOC navigation, thinking blocks, tool call tracking, and skill usage highlighting.</p>
