222	  <!-- 1. Problem + TDD -->
223	  <div class="slide slide-left">
224	    <div class="eyebrow">Why</div>
225	    <h2>LLMs write code —<br>who reviews the reviewer?</h2>
226	    <ul class="step-list" style="margin-top:var(--sp-md)">
227	      <li><span class="step-num">01</span> No trace between a commit and the conversation that produced it</li>
228	      <li><span class="step-num">02</span> Review is reactive — after code lands, not before</li>
229	      <li><span class="step-num">03</span> TDD checks correctness, not behavior quality or UX</li>
230	    </ul>
231	    <div class="table-wrap" style="margin-top:var(--sp-lg)">
232	    <table>
233	      <tr><th></th><th>TDD</th><th>Meta-Harness</th></tr>
234	      <tr><td>Scope</td><td>Code correctness</td><td>Agent behavior + developer experience</td></tr>
235	      <tr><td>Feedback</td><td>Binary: pass / fail</td><td>Qualitative: human AUQ + execution traces</td></tr>
236	      <tr><td>Trigger</td><td>Manual: write test → run</td><td>Auto: git commit/push → hooks fire</td></tr>
237	      <tr><td>Memory</td><td>Test code as spec</td><td>Filesystem: .metaharness/v{version}/</td></tr>
238	      <tr><td>Improvement</td><td>Developer refactors</td><td>Agent diagnoses root cause from traces</td></tr>
239	    </table>
240	    </div>
241	    <div class="keypoint">TDD answers "does it work?" — Meta-Harness answers "is it good?" TDD is necessary but not sufficient for AI-generated code</div>
242	  </div>
